<title>USA: Home Bancorp of Elgin to buy back shares.</title>
<headline>Home Bancorp of Elgin to buy back shares.</headline>
<dateline>ELGIN, Ill. 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Home Bancorp of Elgin Inc said Thursday its board of directors has adopted a program to repurchase up to 350,462 shares, or five percent, of the company's 7 million outstanding common shares.</p>
<p>The program is subject to approval from the Office of Thrift Supervision and will commence as soon as practicable following OTS approval and continue for a period of up to six months, Home Bancorp said.</p>
<p>Home Bancorp shares rose 1/2 to 15-1/2.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
